{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"Dynamic programming counting binary strings of length 14 avoiding runs of 000 or 111 yields 1220.\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of length >=3. Equivalent to sequences where runs of 0 or 1 have length 1 or 2 only. Count via recurrence. Let a_n = number of valid strings length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit. Let b_n = number ending with run of length 2. But need track last bit? Actually runs of 0 or 1 symmetrical. Let A_n = number ending with run length 1 (last bit different from previous). B_n = number ending with run length 2 (last two bits same, third last different or start). Recurrence: For n=1: A_1=2 (0 or1), B_1=0. For n>1: To get A_n: last bit must be different from previous, so previous run can be length1 or2 of opposite bit. So A_n = A_{n-1}+B_{n-1}. For B_n: last two bits same, so previous bit must be same as last, but run length must be 1 before adding same bit. So B_n = A_{n-1}. Because if previous run length 1, adding same bit makes run length 2. Cannot add to run length 2 because would make 3. So recurrence: A_n = A_{n-1}+B_{n-1}, B_n = A_{n-1}. Base: A1=2, B1=0. Compute up to n=14.\n\nLet's compute quickly.\n\nn=1: A=2 B=0 total=2\nn=2: A2 = A1+B1=2+0=2; B2 = A1=2; total=4\nn=3: A3 = A2+B2=2+2=4; B3 = A2=2; total=6\nn=4: A4 = A3+B3=4+2=6; B4 = A3=4; total=10\nn=5: A5 = A4+B4=6+4=10; B5 = A4=6; total=16\nn=6: A6 = 10+6=16; B6 =10; total=26\nn=7: A7 =16+10=26; B7=16; total=42\nn=8: A8=26+16=42; B8=26; total=68\nn=9: A9=42+26=68; B9=42; total=110\nn=10: A10=68+42=110; B10=68; total=178\nn=11: A11=110+68=178; B11=110; total=288\nn=12: A12=178+110=288; B12=178; total=466\nn=13: A13=288+178=466; B13=288; total=754\nn=14: A14=466+288=754; B14=466; total=1220\n\nThus answer 1220. Provide final JSON with decision answer."}}],"created":1790941592,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":759,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4870,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ERksVFTf4kCz35de4nV3MHrd63OaSNJj","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":536.402,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.13047968864023354,"prompt_per_second":7664.028098329237,"predicted_n":759,"predicted_ms":2375.304,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.133646437994723,"predicted_per_second":319.11704775472947}}